cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Asterism in work you publish, please cite the archived version you
  actually ran. A development checkout is not a citable version: only a release
  wheel carries the build identity a result can be traced to.
title: "Asterism: variance-component models for quantitative genetics"
abstract: >-
  Asterism fits variance-component models for quantitative genetics. It takes
  numerical arrays already in memory and returns fit records, profile-likelihood
  intervals and hypothesis tests. The models cover one or several variance
  components, two traits, binary and censored traits, mixed pairs, and
  gene-by-environment interaction with a measured or a binary environment.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Samuel
    family-names: Mathias
    affiliation: >-
      Department of Psychiatry and Behavioral Medicine, Boston Children's
      Hospital
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-0260-0865"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sammosummo/asterism"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.1
# The concept DOI, which always resolves to the newest version. Each paper
# cites the version DOI of the release it actually ran: 10.5281/zenodo.22116963
# for 0.1.1, 10.5281/zenodo.22113715 for 0.1.0.
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22113714"
keywords:
  - quantitative genetics
  - variance components
  - heritability
  - genetic correlation
  - pedigree
